  "description": "KACYOG crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group P 21/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C56 H148 Cl3 Nd5 O32 Zr4,0.5(C4 H8 O1). From the CIF bond table, Nd1 (Nd) has 8 O neighbors; Nd2 (Nd) has 6 O neighbors; Nd3 (Nd) has 6 O neighbors; Nd4 (Nd) has 6 O neighbors; Nd5 (Nd) has 6 O neighbors; Zr1 (Zr) has 6 O neighbors; Zr2 (Zr) has 6 O neighbors; Zr3 (Zr) has 6 O neighbors; Zr4 (Zr) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.595-3.963 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 95.93-113.54°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C56H148Cl3Nd5O32Zr4·0.5(C4H8O). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 2 μ4-O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
